GPL isolation note:
This MIT-licensed main project deliberately keeps GPL components
(LilyPond, MuseScore) in two separate subprojects:
  - render-lilypond/  (GPL-2.0+, see render-lilypond/LICENSE)
  - render-musescore/ (GPL-2.0+, see render-musescore/LICENSE)

These communicate with the main project via HTTP API and MusicXML/MIDI
interchange format, so GPL does NOT "infect" the main codebase.

---

Non-commercial use declaration (v0.4.0+):
The maintainers of mujik-transcriptor commit to using this software for
non-commercial purposes only. This is a statement of intent, not a
legal re-licensing; the code itself remains MIT-licensed for downstream
users who may have different intentions.

If you are a commercial entity, you are advised to:
  1. Review the dependencies you actually pull in (especially extras
     marked `transcribe-*` and `preprocess-*`)
  2. Confirm any model weights (e.g. ByteDance piano MAESTRO checkpoint)
     are compatible with your intended use
  3. Note that this declaration reflects maintainer intent only and
     does not retroactively re-license the MIT code

Rationale: The user/maintainer of mujik-transcriptor uses it for
personal/educational music transcription, and explicitly opts out of
enabling CC-BY-NC-only dependencies (like the standalone
facebookresearch/denoiser) in production paths.
